A||||3||My7Fieros||ECM same for 86 Gt 5 speed/86 GT auto?||||1||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||11-10-2000||01:22 AM||||I suspect the ECM is bad in my 86 Gt auto..Ive got one from an 86 Gt 5 speed...are they the same? Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||11-10-2000||01:47 AM||||I don't think so.  The 5spd chip wouldn't have anything for the TCC on the auto, and a few other differences.  it would work, but it wouldn't drive right. sfaik..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-10-2000||02:25 AM||||YES, the box is the same! All you need to do is change the prom over.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-10-2000||04:52 PM||||Assuming they are both the original ECM then they should be the same model. the model number is on a label on the front of the ECM. (Write the number on the aluminum with something premanent. The label has a habbit of falling off.)<P>The ECM hardware doesn't care what car it's in but the PROM does. The ECM uses the same terminal for the shift light as it does for TC lock. The PROM sets the behavior of that terminal.<P>So you put your automatic PROM into the ECM from the 5 speed it should be just fine. (Do yourself a favor and mark the PROM for the auto so you know which one it is should you drop them while working.)<P>The same would be true of ECMs of the same model retrived from other GM products.||||reg||1
